\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Come, O come, Immanuel,
\par And ransom captive Isreal,
\par That mourns in lonely exile here
\par Until the Son of God appear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par Rejoice !\tab Rejoice !   Immanuel,
\par Shall come thee, O Isreal.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\i0\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O come ,O come, Thou Lord of might,
\par Who to Thy tribes, on Sinai's height,
\par In ancient times didst give the law
\par In cloud, and majesty, and awe.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par Rejoice !\tab Rejoice !   Immanuel,
\par Shall come thee, O Isreal.
\par \i0 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O come, Thou Rod of Jesse, free
\par Thine own from Satan's tyranny;
\par From depths of hell Thy people save,
\par And give them victory o'er the grave.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par Rejoice !\tab Rejoice !   Immanuel,
\par Shall come thee, O Isreal.
\par \i0 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O come, Thou Day-spring, come and cheer
\par Our spirits by Thine advent here ;
\par Disperse the gloomy clouds of night,
\par And death's dark shadows put to flight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par Rejoice !\tab Rejoice !   Immanuel,
\par Shall come thee, O Isreal.
\par \i0 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O come, Thou Key of David, come,
\par And open wide our heavenly home;
\par Make safe the way that leads on high, 
\par And close the path to misery.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par Rejoice !\tab Rejoice !   Immanuel,
\par Shall come thee, O Isreal.
\par \i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
